\pard\sb240\sa100\b\f0\fs34 AT&T AI Immersive Coach - HR1 live demonstration interview packet\b0\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 This document is a truthful walkthrough of the repository as it exists. It does not attribute authorship, claim production integrations that are not configured, or use real HR/student data.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sb180\sa100\b\f0\fs27 Best presentation format: five acts\b0\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 Keep the whole conversation on one memorable spine:\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 1.\tab Outcome: \u8220?Reduce exception-handling time without surrendering human accountability.\u8221?\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 2.\tab Problem: Evidence is fragmented; manual reconciliation is slow and inconsistent.\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 3.\tab Design: Rules first, bounded AI second, human decision last.\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 4.\tab Proof: Run one case, inspect one code path, run the tests.\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 5.\tab Judgment: Name what is production-ready, what is a fixture, and what comes next.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 Use dual-level narration throughout. Give the plain-English sentence first, then the technical proof:\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \u8220?The AI cannot change a record. Technically, the model receives only three read-only function tools, the trace marks writeAccess: false, and no system-of-record write endpoint exists.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 This lets a nontechnical interviewer understand the point while giving the technical leader enough evidence to drill deeper.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sb180\sa100\b\f0\fs27 \u8220?Tell me about yourself\u8221? \u8212? 60 seconds\b0\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 Replace every bracket with a fact from your real resume. Do not invent tenure, employers, metrics, or ownership.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \u8220?I\u8217?m a [current role or professional identity] with [verified years or scope] focused on [two relevant strengths: for example software delivery, AI enablement, technical training, or enterprise integration]. My strength is translating between business outcomes and engineering execution. In [real example], I [specific action] so that [measurable or observable result]. I work by making the problem clear, building a small testable path, and helping people understand not only what to do but why the controls matter. This HR1 workbench reflects that approach: deterministic validation, bounded AI tools, automated tests, and a human decision boundary. I\u8217?m interested in the AI Immersive Coach role because it combines hands-on technical credibility with facilitation\u8212?helping teams move from curiosity to safe, repeatable use of AI.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 If you cannot support a metric, describe the observable outcome without a number. Say \u8220?I led,\u8221? \u8220?I contributed,\u8221? or \u8220?I extended\u8221? only when each is accurate.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sb180\sa100\b\f0\fs27 Trainer/facilitator communication pattern\b0\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 For every major concept, use Define \u8594? Show \u8594? Translate \u8594? Check:\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 1.\tab Define: \u8220?Agentic means the model can choose a tool and use its result in a later reasoning step.\u8221?\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 2.\tab Show: Open runLiveAgent and point to function tools, function_call_output, and the second response.\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 3.\tab Translate: \u8220?That helps with ambiguous exceptions, but the allowlist prevents open-ended access.\u8221?\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 4.\tab Check: \u8220?Would it help if I go deeper on the tool loop or on the governance boundary?\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 If interrupted, answer in four sentences: direct answer, repository evidence, tradeoff, next step. Example:\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \u8220?No, this prototype does not have a database. The current state is synthetic code fixtures and browser-local storage. That makes the demo safe and portable but not suitable for durable enterprise audit. My next step would be an authenticated append-only audit store with retention and access policies.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sb180\sa100\b\f0\fs27 How to address the three interview perspectives\b0\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li180\sa45\f0\fs18 Interviewer perspective    |    What they need to see    |    Evidence to show\par
\pard\li180\sa45\f0\fs18 Technical leader    |    You can reason about architecture, APIs, security, testing, failure modes, and delivery    |    Architecture flow, runLiveAgent, validateAnalysis, negative tests, CI workflows\par
\pard\li180\sa45\f0\fs18 AI coach 1    |    You can explain AI accurately without overwhelming learners    |    Define \u8594? Show \u8594? Translate \u8594? Check pattern; live-mode versus fixture labels\par
\pard\li180\sa45\f0\fs18 AI coach 2    |    You can facilitate adoption and responsible behavior    |    Human-decision boundary, synthetic data, learner checks, fallback plan, gap matrix\par
\pard\li180\sa45\f0\fs18 Entire panel    |    You communicate clearly, command the room, and remain honest    |    Business-first opening, ten-minute structure, direct answers, explicit IMPLEMENTED/PARTIAL/NOT FOUND/UNKNOWN language\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 Do not run three separate presentations. Tell one story and briefly change depth for the person asking the question.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sb180\sa100\b\f0\fs27 What to say first\b0\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \u8220?I\u8217?ll demonstrate this as a governed AI integration workbench, not as an autonomous decision-maker. The business problem is fragmented evidence and slow exception handling. The engineering answer is deterministic validation first, bounded AI tools only for the residual ambiguity, strict output checks, and an authorized person making the final decision. I\u8217?ll show the architecture, run one synthetic case end to end, then prove the controls with tests.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 That opening serves both audiences: leaders hear the outcome and boundary; engineers hear the control strategy.\par
\pard\sa70\par
