\pard\sb180\sa100\b\f0\fs27 Two-minute architectural walkthrough\b0\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 Use this almost word for word:\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \u8220?The frontend is a dependency-light static application: HTML for semantics, CSS for responsive presentation, and JavaScript for state and API orchestration. Its entry point is the DOMContentLoaded handler in app.js, which renders the workbench and checks the backend execution mode.\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \u8220?For this demo, the browser submits only an allowlisted synthetic case ID to POST /api/interview/analyze. The Node backend rejects arbitrary records, runs deterministic comparison first, and chooses a clearly labeled execution path. Without model configuration it uses a deterministic server fixture. With model configuration, runLiveAgent uses the Responses API and lets the model select only three read-only tools. Policy still forces every required check to run.\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \u8220?The second model response must satisfy a strict JSON schema. validateAnalysis rejects unsupported evidence IDs and requires the exact human-decision boundary. The frontend shows the tool trace and recommendation, but disables decision recording until a human adds rationale. The demo audit is intentionally browser-local; a production system would use an authenticated durable audit store.\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 \u8220?Operationally, Caddy serves immutable static releases and proxies /api to Azure Functions. CI validates source, runs API tests, builds hashed assets, and validates the deployable artifact. The current repo has no enterprise database or live system-of-record writeback, and I state those gaps explicitly.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
