\pard\sb180\sa100\b\f0\fs27 30 likely technical questions and evidence-based answers\b0\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 1.\tab What is the frontend framework? No framework: semantic HTML, responsive CSS, and browser JavaScript. Evidence: index.html, styles.css, and the DOMContentLoaded entry in app.js.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 2.\tab What is the backend? Node.js Azure Functions v4 using CommonJS. api/package.json points main to src/index.js; api/src/index.js registers the HTTP functions.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 3.\tab Why no React? The prototype does not require component-runtime complexity. The dependency-light frontend reduces build and supply-chain surface. For a larger team/product, component reuse and browser tests could justify a framework.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 4.\tab What database does it use? None. Synthetic cases are code fixtures; UI decisions use localStorage through saveState and renderInterviewAudit. Durable enterprise audit storage is not implemented.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 5.\tab What are the API endpoints? security/status, security/csrf, security/scan, interview/status, and interview/analyze, registered in api/src/index.js under the Azure Functions /api prefix.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 6.\tab Walk me through one AI request. runInterviewAnalysis posts an allowlisted ID. createInterviewHandlers.analyze validates origin/rate/case, runs deterministic tools, optionally calls runLiveAgent, validates output, and returns a request ID, trace, and recommendation.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 7.\tab What makes this agentic? Only live-model mode: the model can choose among function tools, receive their outputs, and produce a subsequent structured response. That loop is in runLiveAgent. A single prompt/response and both guided fixtures are not described as agentic.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 8.\tab Which tools can the model use? load_case_evidence, compare_case_fields, and get_governance_policy, defined by toolDefinitions and executed by executeTool in api/src/interviewAssistant.js.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 9.\tab Can the agent mutate records? No. No write tool exists; trace entries report writeAccess: false; output requires human review. Enterprise writeback is not implemented.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 10.\tab How is the loop bounded? MAX_MODEL_TOOL_CALLS is three, case IDs are enumerated, tools are strict, and the second model request sets tool_choice: "none".\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 11.\tab How do you control hallucinations? validateAnalysis permits only known recommendations, bounds confidence, validates arrays, rejects citations outside the computed evidence allowlist, and requires the exact decision boundary.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 12.\tab Why deterministic rules before AI? Exact comparisons are cheaper, testable, and explainable. compareSyntheticCase produces matches, differences, critical differences, confidence, and a recommendation before the model is used.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 13.\tab What happens without a model key? modelMode selects guided-fixture; the UI labels it Server guided fixture. If the API is absent, the UI labels Browser guided fixture. Neither is presented as model output.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 14.\tab How are model secrets handled? configFromEnvironment reads server environment variables. OPENAI_API_KEY is absent from frontend artifacts and is checked by securityAssurance.test.js. The runbook recommends ignored local settings and Azure Key Vault references.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 15.\tab How is authentication implemented? Admin security scans use Entra JWT verification through createTokenVerifier, remote JWKS, issuer/audience checks, and an application role. The synthetic interview analysis is public but tightly allowlisted and read-only.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 16.\tab How is CSRF handled? The admin scan uses origin validation plus a double-submit token from security/csrf; createSecurityHandlers.scan compares the cookie and X-HR1-CSRF header.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 17.\tab How is CORS handled? Production accepts the public origin; interview local origins are enabled only when NODE_ENV is development or test. See allowedOrigin in interviewAssistant.js.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 18.\tab What prevents abuse? Case allowlisting, small request shape, 16 KB local adapter body cap, upstream timeouts, tool limit, no write tools, and in-memory per-IP rate limiting. Distributed rate limiting remains a production gap.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 19.\tab How are upstream errors exposed? Handlers return generic codes such as analysis_unavailable or status_unavailable and log a request ID/category without raw provider responses or credentials.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 20.\tab How is the AI branch tested without cost? interviewAssistant.test.js injects fetchImpl and returns fake Responses API payloads. Tests cover tool calls and the structured second response without network access.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 21.\tab What other tests exist? securityAssurance.test.js covers status sanitization, documented response mapping, auth/role checks, CSRF, fixed scan payload, rate limiting, malformed results, upstream errors, and secret absence in static artifacts.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 22.\tab What is not tested? There is no automated browser E2E/visual-regression suite, load test, model-quality evaluation set, or deployed-environment integration test.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 23.\tab How does the build work? scripts/build.sh copies source/assets into dist and adds content hashes to CSS/JS URLs. scripts/verify.mjs checks required language and positioning.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 24.\tab How is it deployed? .github/workflows/deploy.yml builds static assets and atomically switches a Hetzner release. .github/workflows/deploy-security-api.yml tests and deploys api/ to Azure Functions when enabled.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 25.\tab How does routing work in production? deployment/Caddyfile.hr1 serves static files and reverse-proxies /api/* to Azure Functions, preserving same-origin browser requests.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 26.\tab What Microsoft APIs are real? graphGet calls Microsoft Graph /me and /me/drive/root/children after delegated MSAL sign-in. Broader Teams, SharePoint, SIS, LMS, HR, and finance integrations are architecture/design unless configured elsewhere.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 27.\tab How do you address privacy? Interview cases are explicitly synthetic, the browser sends only an allowlisted ID, no model tool can access arbitrary records, and outputs are not authoritative decisions. A real rollout would still require data classification, retention, legal review, and access audits.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 28.\tab How do you observe a request? The API creates a UUID request ID and logs completion/failure category, case ID, mode, and duration. Full distributed tracing/dashboard verification is not present.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 29.\tab What does Git history prove? It shows an incremental sequence of architecture and UI commits (git log --oneline). It establishes repository evolution, not who personally authored every line or whether every feature was production-operated.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 30.\tab What would you build next? Durable authenticated audit storage, distributed throttling, browser E2E tests, formal AI evals, and one authorized read-only enterprise connector before any controlled writeback.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sb180\sa100\b\f0\fs27 10 likely coaching and behavioral questions\b0\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs21 Use your own real example wherever brackets appear.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 1.\tab Why this AI Immersive Coach role? \u8220?It sits at the intersection where I add the most value: I can build and inspect the technology, explain it at the learner\u8217?s altitude, and turn responsible-AI principles into repeatable engineering behavior. This demo shows all three.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 2.\tab Why AT&T? \u8220?The role calls for both technical depth and the ability to help people adopt AI through practical experiences. I am attracted to work where scale makes clarity, safety, APIs, testing, and change management equally important.\u8221? Do not add unverified claims about AT&T strategy.\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 3.\tab How do you teach a mixed technical/nontechnical audience? \u8220?I use one shared business scenario, explain each concept in plain language, then offer technical depth as a second layer. I ask brief check questions and let advanced learners inspect code without losing beginners.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 4.\tab How would you explain agentic AI to a beginner? \u8220?A normal model call is question in, answer out. An agentic workflow can choose an approved tool, observe the result, and continue toward a goal. The important engineering work is limiting the tools, loop, data, and authority.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 5.\tab What do you do when a live demo fails? \u8220?I name the failure accurately, move to the designed fallback, and preserve the learning objective. Here the badge distinguishes live model, server fixture, and browser fixture; then I prove the contract with an automated test.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 6.\tab How do you handle a skeptical engineer? \u8220?I invite falsification. We inspect the boundary, run the negative tests, and review the exact gaps. I do not ask them to trust a slide when the code can prove or disprove the claim.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 7.\tab How do you keep learners engaged? \u8220?I alternate explanation with prediction and action: ask what should happen, run the case, inspect why it happened, then change one small behavior. That turns a passive demo into a coached engineering experience.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 8.\tab How do you measure coaching effectiveness? \u8220?I use behavior and outcome measures: can learners explain the boundary, complete the task without prompting, write a meaningful test, identify a risk, and transfer the pattern to a new use case? In a real program I would establish baseline and follow-up measures.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 9.\tab Tell us about influencing without authority. Use STAR: Situation [real cross-team constraint]; Task [shared outcome]; Action [how you listened, translated concerns, created evidence, and facilitated a decision]; Result [verified outcome]; Reflection [what you improved next time].\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\li540\fi-300\sa55\f0\fs21 10.\tab What would your first 30/60/90 days look like? \u8220?First 30: listen, learn the audience, governance, tooling, and success measures. By 60: co-facilitate and improve one hands-on module using learner evidence. By 90: independently lead an experience, publish reusable patterns, and report adoption, skill, and safety outcomes.\u8221?\par
\pard\sa70\par
\pard\sb180\sa100\b\f0\fs27 Risk and gap matrix\b0\par
\pard\sa70\par
